{
  "version": 3,
  "title": "What if your plane blew up?",
  "series": "Freefall / Pick Your Landing",
  "narration": "Your plane exploded. No warning, no parachute, just sky. First the sky takes your mind, up here there isn't enough oxygen, your vision narrows, you pass out mid-scream. But falling air thickens, and at ten thousand feet you're wide awake again. Tumbling at a hundred and twenty miles an hour, wind screaming, you get to pick where this ends. Look down. A river, a forest, a rocky field, a plowed farm. The river lies, water at this speed hits like concrete. Trees can break your fall, if you're lucky with the branches. Rocks are just rocks. So arch your back, spread your arms, kill the spin, and steer for the farm. Five thousand feet, two thousand, five hundred. Feet first, knees bent, and roll. You hit the wheat, pop up, brush off your jacket, and walk away. Next time? Take the train.",
